The link provided in the GitHub instructions for the online tutorial did not work. Therefore, I used this link as an alternative: https://learn.arcgis.com/en/projects/analyze-volcano-shelter-access-in-hawaii/. I used this link to complete Task 1 to make the Hawaii map.

Link to the mapping application: https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/68f5ec66dd7c4ad383126aca80ecab54.

Because the Collector app has been retired, I attempted to use the Field Map app instead: https://www.esri.com/en-us/arcgis/products/arcgis-field-maps/downloads.
Since this app does not allow me to view the Experience map, I took two screenshots. One screenshot is of the Experience map online, and the other screenshot is of the Web Map in the app. 
